{% comment %}
  Therapy booking — FLOW CHANGE per explicit instruction (node 539:2128):
  this screen is no longer "pick the one doctor, then a date/time" — it's
  now Step 1 of a new 2-step therapy flow, "Choose your therapy": either
  pick a specific therapy from a (decorative, not-yet-wired) dropdown, OR
  pick a broader therapy category from a checkbox list below an "OR"
  divider. The old doctor card + date-strip + time-slot-grid content for
  this step is deleted entirely, not hidden/kept around — this is a
  genuinely different screen, not a restyle of the old one.

  Consequences of deleting the old content, cleaned up alongside it:
  - kal-booking-flow.js's whole therapy day/slot-picking machinery
    (therapySlot state, renderTherapyDayStrip, renderTherapySlotPeriods,
    fetchTherapySlotsForDate, loadTherapySlotDay, updateTherapyContinueButton)
    is gone — nothing on this screen fetches or picks a date/time anymore.
  - The calendar modal (kal-booking-flow.liquid's kal-calendar-modal) was
    ONLY ever opened by this screen's old calendar-icon button (the
    Consultation Slot Picker's own calendar icon is decorative-only, see
    that step's liquid comment) — with this screen's button gone too,
    nothing opens it anymore, so the modal markup/CSS/JS is removed
    entirely rather than left dead.
  - The date/slot helpers those functions were the only callers of
    (toDateKey, formatDayChipLabel, DAY_LABELS, SLOT_PERIODS, STRIP_DAYS,
    MAX_FUTURE_DAYS, maxFutureDate, periodForHour, generateMockSlots) are
    removed from kal-booking-flow.js too — see that file's own comments.
    addDays/todayStart/formatTime12h/formatConfirmationDate/
    CONSULT_DURATION_MINUTES stay: Confirmation's summary and the
    Consultation Slot Picker's static day-chip click handler still use
    those.

  Header uses the same shared kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid as the
  consultation flow (back/facility badge/close + step progress bar) —
  step_total is 2 here, not 5, and next_label is "Personal details"
  (Step 2 of 2, not yet built — see the Continue button's own comment
  below).

  Therapy category selection reuses the exact same checkbox-row pattern
  and CSS as Concern Select (.kal-concern-row and friends) for visual
  consistency, but with its own separate data attribute/state
  (data-kal-therapy-concern, therapyConcernSelect in
  kal-booking-flow.js) — deliberately not sharing Concern Select's own
  concernSelect state, since these are two different selections in two
  different flows that happen to look alike.

  The "Select the therapy" dropdown is now a real multi-select (node
  623:7334, the open-panel state of this same dropdown), not decorative —
  explicit instruction. THERAPY_OPTIONS in kal-booking-flow.js is the
  static list of ~17 named therapies (with a couple carrying a "Most
  Booked"/"Featured" tag, matching the export); the panel itself
  (data-kal-therapy-dropdown-list) is rendered client-side by
  renderTherapyDropdownList() rather than hardcoded here, since its whole
  point is to re-sort on every toggle — selected items move to the top of
  the list (explicit instruction), which is far simpler as a re-render
  than as DOM node reordering.

  Confirm is hidden until at least one therapy is selected — EITHER a
  specific one from this dropdown OR a category checkbox below (explicit
  instruction: "minimum 1 concern should be selected to show the confirm
  cta", same rule Concern Select already uses, just now checking two
  selection sets instead of one — see updateTherapyConcernContinueButton()
  in kal-booking-flow.js).

  Not yet wired into the main flow's navigation — there's no preceding
  "which facility" step and no defined Step 2 of 2 ("Personal details")
  yet. data-kal-back defaults to "entry" as a reasonable placeholder
  until the actual preceding screen is defined, same as before. The
  Confirm button has no data-kal-goto yet for the same reason — it just
  enables/shows once something is picked, with nowhere to navigate to
  until Step 2 of 2 exists. Button text is "Confirm" (not "Continue"),
  matching this node's own footer.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-therapy-slot kal-step-shell kal-step-shell--progress-panel" data-kal-doctor-id="0f425bd1-9a69-4adc-a0a3-6f2b8ba87191" data-kal-facility-id="185b85d7-fad2-405d-b8ea-13dc683fbde8">

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop left column — same 300px "Selected Clinic" + "Your Progress"
    pattern as the consultation flow's own progress-panel steps (Concern
    Select/Doctor Select/Slot Picker/Patient Details/Confirmation), reused
    here for this therapy flow's own 2 steps instead of a parallel
    layout. kal-booking-flow-step-progress.liquid's own step_names param
    (added for this) is what lets the SAME stepper component show
    "Choose therapy"/"Personal details" here instead of the 5-step
    consultation list.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-concern-select__info">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__info-scroll">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-header">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-concern-select__heading">Therapy Request</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-section">
        <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Selected Clinic</p>
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-facility-picker', step_number: 1, location_text: 'Indiranagar', extra_class: 'kal-concern-select__info-pill' -%}
      </div>

      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 1, step_names: 'Choose therapy|Personal details' -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'entry', step_number: 1, step_total: 2, next_label: 'Personal details' -%}

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
        "Selected therapies" chip list (node 623:7592) — a summary of the
        SAME therapyDropdownSelect state as the dropdown below, shown as
        removable pills above the fold so a selection is visible without
        opening the dropdown. Hidden entirely until ≥1 therapy is picked;
        rendered/re-rendered client-side by renderTherapySelectedChips() in
        kal-booking-flow.js, called alongside renderTherapyDropdownList()
        everywhere the dropdown selection changes. "Clear all" here is the
        single global control (the dropdown panel below has no instance
        of its own) — data-kal-therapy-dropdown-clear calls
        clearTherapyDropdownSelection().
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-therapy-selected" data-kal-therapy-selected hidden>
        <div class="kal-therapy-selected__head">
          <p class="kal-therapy-selected__title">Selected therapies</p>
          <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-selected__clear" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-clear>Clear all</button>
        </div>
        <div class="kal-therapy-selected__chips" data-kal-therapy-selected-chips></div>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose your therapy</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-therapy-select-wrapper" data-kal-therapy-dropdown>
        <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-select" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Select the therapy">
          <span class="kal-therapy-select__placeholder" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-label>Select the therapy</span>
          <span class="kal-therapy-select__chevron" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-down' -%}
          </span>
        </button>

        {%- comment -%} Rows populated/re-sorted client-side — see this file's own top comment {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-therapy-dropdown" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-panel hidden>
          <div class="kal-therapy-dropdown__head">
            <span class="kal-therapy-dropdown__title">All Therapies</span>
            {%- comment -%}
              No "Clear all" here — the "Selected therapies" chip list's
              own instance above (data-kal-therapy-dropdown-clear on
              .kal-therapy-selected__clear) is the single global control
              per explicit instruction.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="kal-therapy-dropdown__summary" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-summary hidden>
              <span data-kal-therapy-dropdown-count>0 selected</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-therapy-dropdown__list" data-kal-therapy-dropdown-list></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-therapy-divider">
        <span class="kal-therapy-divider__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="kal-therapy-divider__text">OR</span>
        <span class="kal-therapy-divider__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <p class="kal-therapy-category-label">Choose a therapy category</p>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__list">
        <button type="button" class="kal-concern-row" data-kal-therapy-concern="relaxation-stress-relief" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
            <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'concern-therapy' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-row__name">Relaxation &amp; Stress Relief</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-concern-row" data-kal-therapy-concern="pain-management" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
            <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'concern-therapy' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-row__name">Pain Management</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-concern-row" data-kal-therapy-concern="beauty-skin-care" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
            <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'concern-therapy' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-row__name">Beauty &amp; Skin Care</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-concern-row" data-kal-therapy-concern="physiotherapy-rehab" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
            <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'concern-therapy' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-row__name">Physiotherapy &amp; Rehab</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
          </span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-concern-row" data-kal-therapy-concern="therapeutic-massage" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
            <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'concern-therapy' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-row__name">Therapeutic Massage</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden until a category or a specific therapy is picked — see
      updateTherapyConcernContinueButton() in kal-booking-flow.js, which
      generically toggles EVERY element with data-kal-therapy-concern-footer/
      data-kal-therapy-concern-continue/data-kal-therapy-concern-summary,
      so this mobile instance and the desktop one below stay in sync with
      zero JS changes. Confirm/Continue's click behavior is handled
      explicitly in kal-booking-flow.js (not a plain data-kal-goto — see
      that file's own comment on why), so both instances share that same
      hook too.

      The summary line above the button is conditional, not just a plain
      "N selected" — explicit instruction: it only appears once at least
      one CATEGORY is picked (either alone, or combined with dropdown
      therapies, e.g. "2 therapies & 1 therapy category selected"). When
      only specific therapies are picked from the dropdown with no
      category, this stays hidden — that case is already communicated by
      the dropdown's own trigger label ("N therapy selected", see
      updateTherapyDropdownSummary()), so a second count here would be
      redundant. See updateTherapyConcernContinueButton() for the exact text.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--mobile" data-kal-therapy-concern-footer hidden>
      <p class="kal-therapy-concern-summary" data-kal-therapy-concern-summary hidden></p>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-therapy-concern-continue>
        Confirm
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop-only full-width footer bar, same pattern as the consultation
    flow's progress-panel steps — help text + Back/Continue split across
    the shared 300px/1fr grid columns. Continue keeps the exact same
    data-kal-therapy-concern-continue hook as the mobile instance (see
    that button's own comment above).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--desktop" data-kal-therapy-concern-footer hidden>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-help kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-actions">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back kal-concern-select__footer-back" data-kal-back="entry" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        <span>Back</span>
      </button>
      {%- comment -%}
        Desktop's own summary + Confirm stack — mobile has this same
        summary line in its own footer above (see that instance's own
        comment); this is a second instance of the SAME element
        (data-kal-therapy-concern-summary), kept in sync by the generic
        querySelectorAll('[data-kal-therapy-concern-summary]') loop in
        updateTherapyConcernContinueButton().
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-therapy-concern-desktop-continue">
        <p class="kal-therapy-concern-summary" data-kal-therapy-concern-summary hidden></p>
        <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-therapy-concern-continue>
          Confirm
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
